// Cycle of Life: Realistic Fauna - Legacy of the Phanerozoic: Shovel Mouth (hadrosauroidea).
//
// TWENTY-SEVEN hadrosauroids, the largest single file in this series, from a 14 tonne
// Shangtungosaurus to a 600 kg Secernosaurus, plus their nests. These are the cattle of the
// Cretaceous - abundant, herding, and the prey base that everything else in the series eats.
//
// 1. THEY EAT NOTHING AS SHIPPED. Eighth mod running with an empty foodCategories list and a lone
//    "fruitmash" tag. Given Vegetable + Fruit throughout: hadrosaurs had the most sophisticated
//    chewing apparatus of any dinosaur, dental batteries of hundreds of teeth grinding tough plant
//    matter, and BRACHYLOPHOSAURUS confirms what that was for - the mummified specimen called
//    Leonardo preserved stomach contents of ferns, conifers and magnolias. That is the fourth animal
//    in this series with a diet known directly rather than inferred, after the ankylosaur ferns, the
//    Deinocheirus fish and the Isaberrysaura cycad seeds.
//
// 2. BODY WEIGHT, FLAT 4000 kg PER ADULT - and here the hitboxes are no help at all, since the mod
//    draws twenty-six of the twenty-seven at an identical 2 x 3. The fossil record does all the work.
//    Four tonnes happens to be about right for the mid-sized crested forms and is three times too
//    light for Shangtungosaurus and five times too heavy for Secernosaurus.
//
// 3. MAIASAURA IS THE ONE ANIMAL IN THIS PACK WITH LOWERED JUVENILE MORTALITY, and it earns it. The
//    name means good mother lizard, given for the first solid evidence of dinosaur PARENTAL CARE:
//    colonial nesting grounds where hatchlings stayed in the nest and were fed. Juvenile mortality is
//    what that behaviour actually changes, so it is set to 0.7 against the family default of 0.88.
//    Every other file in this series uses one number for the whole family; this is the exception the
//    evidence justifies.
//
// 4. HERDS. Hadrosaurs are the herding dinosaurs, and the bone beds are enormous. EDMONTOSAURUS is
//    known from beds holding thousands of individuals and MAIASAURA from nesting colonies of similar
//    scale; both take the largest herds. Island dwarfs and fragmentary taxa get smaller groups.
//
//    Also worth noting on Edmontosaurus: one specimen carries a HEALED TYRANNOSAUR BITE on its tail.
//    An animal that was attacked by the largest predator of its world and walked away from it.
//
// 5. THEY ARE PREY, and nothing here defends itself the way the ankylosaurs, stegosaurs and
//    ceratopsians do - no clubs, no spikes, no horns. Predation vulnerability runs high across the
//    file, moderated only by size. This is the food that makes the carnivore mods in this series
//    viable, and their hunt lists all name hadrosauroidea explicitly.
//
// NESTS ARE CHAIN SEEDS, as elsewhere in the series. Only INCUBATING nests need entries; mature and
// empty get triesPerChunk 0, and eggs are runtime chance 0.0.
//
// VERIFICATION STATUS: keys derived from the mod own entity JSON, not read off a live roster - this
// mod is not installed on the pack author server. A wrong key is inert (the entry is ignored and the
// animal keeps its auto-discovered values); `/col species` lists the authoritative keys.
